## 7. DETAILED ORGAN, CELL, AND ORGANELE EXPLORER

This is a core educational feature.

Whenever a student clicks a supported organ, cell, organelle, or meaningful biological structure, open a dedicated detail page or a clearly separate detailed view.

Examples:
- Plant Cell → Mitochondrion
- Plant Cell → Chloroplast
- Plant Cell → Nucleus
- Human Heart → Relevant heart structure
- Neuron → Dendrite, cell body, axon, or another supported structure
- Nephron → Relevant nephron structure

### Every detail page should include, where scientifically applicable:
- Bengali name
- English scientific name
- Accurate labelled diagram or 3D model
- Location within the larger organ, cell, or organism
- Main structural components
- Functions of the whole structure
- Functions of its internal components
- How the structure works
- Relevant biological processes
- Simple Bengali explanation
- Important SSC-level facts
- Related topics and diagrams
- Link to the parent structure
- Related important questions

### Example: Mitochondrion

A student selects the mitochondrion in a plant-cell diagram.

Open a dedicated mitochondrion detail page or view containing:
- Outer membrane
- Inner membrane
- Intermembrane space, where appropriate
- Cristae
- Matrix
- Functions of the relevant components
- Cellular respiration and ATP production
- A scientifically accurate labelled diagram
- A rotating/zoomable 3D model if available
- Related SSC Biology explanations and questions

The internal components should themselves be selectable when the model and implementation genuinely support selection.

Do not create empty detail pages with only a title.

Do not pretend that an ordinary static picture supports clickable substructures. If a static picture cannot safely be modified, preserve it and provide accurate external labels, a legend, or a separate interactive diagram.

### Whole-cell diagram-label rule

For whole-cell diagrams, Bengali labels should appear OUTSIDE the illustration, alongside the existing English labels where practical, with leader lines pointing to the correct structures.

Do not place large Bengali label boxes or markers over the cell itself if they obstruct the structures.

Maintain readable labels, correct leader-line targets, and a clear diagram.

### Scientific accuracy

Do not invent biological structures, functions, or labels.

Use the applicable textbook and reliable scientific references when verifying uncertain details. If a requested detail is outside the SSC syllabus, clearly distinguish it as additional learning material.

